              <td>{ckOff.outputs.join(', ')}</td>
              <td>{ckOff.licence}</td>
              <td><a href={ckOff.weights?.url}>les_fit</a></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="small">
        From <Cite id="kim2025les" locator="MACELES-OFF section; Table II; Data availability" />. The 4G-HDNNPs of Ko et al. and the CACE-LR models of the
        LES papers are fitted to one system each (training scripts and models for the latter are in the les_fit repository); they are not
        general-purpose checkpoints and are not listed. The <a href="/models/checkpoints/">checkpoints page</a> lists every recorded checkpoint.
      </p>
      <Callout kind="note" title="Related families">
        <a href="/models/behler-parrinello/">Behler–Parrinello</a> networks are the 2G ancestor of the 4G-HDNNP. <a href="/models/grace/">GRACE</a>
        shares CACE’s cluster-expansion basis in spherical form. <a href="/models/mace/">MACE</a> hosts LES in MACELES-OFF, and
        <a href="/models/esen-uma/">UMA</a> takes total charge and spin as inputs for molecules instead of computing electrostatics.
      </Callout>
    </section>

